# CIDRella: sudoers file for the cidrella service account.
#
# As of v0.4.14, this file is EMPTY. Every sudo callsite has been eliminated:
#
# - v0.4.11: in-app updater and dnsmasq reload/restart replaced with
#   polkit-gated systemctl (D-Bus, no setuid escalation needed).
#
# - v0.4.14: arping replaced with a direct execFile call. The cidrella
#   service runs with AmbientCapabilities=CAP_NET_RAW (set by
#   cidrella.service), which propagates to child processes on exec,
#   including arping. No sudo, no setcap, no file capabilities on the
#   arping binary. Verified on testerella via a transient systemd unit
#   running as the cidrella user with AmbientCapabilities=CAP_NET_RAW.
#
# The file is kept (rather than deleted) so that install.sh's `cp ...
# /etc/sudoers.d/cidrella` doesn't fail on upgrade, and so the empty
# file actively overwrites any stale sudoers rules from prior versions.
